<?xml version="1.0" encoding="UTF-8"?>
<!--
    Parses this proxy's XML-DSig signing config, loaded from the shared
    KVM "signature" (entry key "{apiproxy.name}.xmldsig.sign"), into a
    flow variable. The KVM entry value is a JSON object, e.g.:
      {
        "certificatePem": "[PEM BEGIN CERTIFICATE marker]\nMIIDGTCC...\n[PEM END CERTIFICATE marker]\n"
      }
      (an actual entry has real PEM "BEGIN/END CERTIFICATE" dashed
      markers — spelled out here as bracketed placeholders only because a
      run of dashes isn't legal inside an XML comment)

    certificatePem is required (IgnoreUnresolvedVariables=false): a JSON
    string can hold literal "\n" escapes for the multi-line PEM, and this
    JSONPath extraction is EXPECTED to unescape them back into real
    newlines the way JC-Assemble-XmlDsig-Signature's CertificateFactory
    parsing needs — but confirm that on your actual Apigee version rather
    than trusting this comment: that assumption was documented here
    without having been verified against a live instance, and a real
    failure traced back to exactly this gap. JC-Assemble-XmlDsig-Signature
    now normalizes literal "\n"/"\r\n"/"\r" sequences defensively before
    parsing (see its class comment), so a wrong assumption here no longer
    breaks signing — but if VerifyJWS ever rejects a KVM-configured
    public key that looks correct (signature.verify.jwt.publicKey.pem,
    parsed the same way in SF-Signature-Validator), the same gap is the
    first thing to check there, since that path has no Java callout to
    add the same normalization to.

    signature.xmldsig.certificate.pem feeds
    JC-Assemble-XmlDsig-Signature's "certificate-pem" Property directly.
-->
<ExtractVariables name="EV-XmlDsig-Sign-Parse-Config">
    <DisplayName>EV-XmlDsig-Sign-Parse-Config</DisplayName>
    <Source>signature.xmldsig.sign.config.json</Source>
    <JSONPayload>
        <Variable name="signature.xmldsig.certificate.pem" type="string">
            <JSONPath>$.certificatePem</JSONPath>
        </Variable>
    </JSONPayload>
    <IgnoreUnresolvedVariables>false</IgnoreUnresolvedVariables>
</ExtractVariables>
